# One of two targets becoming illegal (CR 608.2b) and the source leaving (CR 113.7a): on turn three the combat trigger
# targets Bishop and Bot2's Ornithopter, and Bot2 answers with Lightning Bolt on Bishop. Bishop dies; the trigger is
# independent of its source, so it still resolves and Ornithopter, still a legal target, gets its counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Agent Bishop, Man in Black
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Agent Bishop, Man in Black.Cast
Bot1.Target(Agent Bishop, Man in Black; Ornithopter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Agent Bishop, Man in Black)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Agent Bishop, Man in Black
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
